 "notes": [
  "E10 multi-seed rerun of the I8-orchestrated real-gateway cache experiment at the reduced scale sanctioned by the task instruction: --tasks 100 --seeds 2 (paper protocol: --tasks 200 --seeds 1).",
  "Honest scale annotation: with 100 tasks per (zipf, seed) the workload contains fewer repeated (instruction, params) pairs than the paper's 200-task runs, so hit rates and call reductions are NOT comparable 1:1 to the frozen paper numbers; the per-zipf side-by-side is provided for context only.",
  "Two seeds per zipf bucket give a real (if small) stdev; single-number cells would have stdev 0.0 by convention. The 5-seed protocol of the synthetic suite was not affordable on the real gateway within this session (each round trip costs ~2 s; 5 seeds x 3 zipf x ~192 calls would exceed the session budget).",
  "Per-call latency p50, wall times and token counts come from the gateway's own usage/latency measurements; no simulated values in this run."
 ],
